  "summary": "Senior at the University of Washington studying electrical engineering with a concentration in embedded systems graduating in December of 2017. Seeking an entry-level/intern position in a computing/high-technology company where I can apply my experience with embedded and real-time systems under an OPT status. \n\nThrough multiple labs in class, I've gained understanding of C/C++ programming in the Linux environment and is familiar with working with Bash while working with a Beaglebone Black and numerous peripherals. On top of that, I am familiar with FPGA programming languages such as Verilog and have completed multiple projects with an Altera DeSoc board. I also have a great interest in software programming and have taken multiple programming courses outside of my major requirements, such as Data Structure and Algorithms, C language, and Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning. \n\nDuring my four years in college, I was a part of the Taiwanese Student Association (TSA), and served as the Secretary and Vice President for one year respectively. My duties consisted of organizing and taking meeting minutes, event planning, officer recruitment, conflict resolution, and job distribution. Through this, I've become more detail-oriented and more confident with my leadership skills. Though I started off college as a soft-spoken freshman, TSA has given me the opportunity to evolve into a senior with leadership skills.  \n\nMy technical skills include:\n- Programming: C/C++, Java, Python,  Verilog, MATLAB, Linux Bash\n- Circuit theory and circuit simulation software such as LT Spice\n- Real time embedded systems\n- Computer architecture \n- Basic PCB design",
